The single source is AB 88 (2023-2024), chaptered 2023-10-13, digest line "AB 88, Sanchez." — her own act (`record` / `author`), in-term, and I quoted the operative victim-notice provision as `provision_quote`.

It fails V2. The ladder asks how the system should respond to someone who breaks the law, and the rungs separate support/treatment from real consequences. AB 88's operative sections give crime victims a 15-day route to be heard at resentencing and cap the notice the department may require before a parole hearing. That governs who gets to speak at a hearing, not what the system does to the offender — it sets no penalty, no consequence, and no treatment. `adjacent` on V2, `off-axis` on V4, so no passage survives and the row is blank.

